        "created_at": "2025-09-05T12:11:59.759Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Greetings, Fellow Capsuleers!</p>\n<p>I have created an Model Content Protocol (MCP) tool for the Eve Swagger Interface API.</p>\n<p>It definitely will need some love, but it should be able to add multiple characters and perform actions based on authenticated characters, without any manual insertion. Everything is performed via MCP tool calling.</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox githubrepo\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/unclemusclez/EveOnlineMCP\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/unclemusclez/EveOnlineMCP\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">github.com</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <div class=\"github-row\" data-github-private-repo=\"false\">\n  <span class=\"broken-image\" title=\"This image is broken\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-link-slash svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#link-slash\"></use></svg></span>\n\n  <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/unclemusclez/EveOnlineMCP\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">GitHub - unclemusclez/EveOnlineMCP:  A local MCP server for accessing the EVE Online...</a></h3>\n\n    <p><span class=\"github-repo-description\"> A local MCP server for accessing the EVE Online ESI API</span></p>\n</div>\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n",
